{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-234491d9fe82c27ab445","statement":"(q^{-1}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{kji})z_{kj}=(\\kappa_{kji}+1)(\\lambda_{jk}^{-1}\\kappa_{kji}+q^{-1}[\\lambda_{jk};0])\n\n(q^{-1}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{kji})z_{ji}=\\kappa_{kji}(\\lambda_{ij}\\kappa_{kji}-[\\lambda_{ij};-1])\n\n(q^{2}\\lambda_{ij}+(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{kij})z_{ki}=(\\kappa_{kij}+q\\lambda_{ij})(q^{-1}\\lambda_{jk}\\kappa_{kij}+q[\\lambda_{ik};0])\n\n(q^{2}\\lambda_{ij}+(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{kij})z_{ij}=\\kappa_{kij}(q^{-1}\\kappa_{kij}+[\\lambda_{ij};1])\n\n(q^{-2}\\lambda_{jk}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{ikj})z_{ik}=(\\kappa_{ikj}+q^{-1}\\lambda_{jk})(q\\lambda_{ij}\\kappa_{ikj}-q^{-1}[\\lambda_{ik};0])\n\n(q^{-2}\\lambda_{jk}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{ikj})z_{kj}=\\kappa_{ikj}(q\\kappa_{ikj}-[\\lambda_{jk};-1])\n\n(q\\lambda_{jk}^{-1}+(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{jki})z_{jk}=(\\kappa_{jki}+\\lambda_{jk}^{-1})(\\kappa_{jki}-q[\\lambda_{jk};0])\n\n(q\\lambda_{jk}^{-1}+(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{jki})z_{ki}=\\kappa_{jki}(\\lambda_{ij}^{-1}\\kappa_{jki}-[\\lambda_{ik};-1])\n\n(q^{-1}\\lambda_{ij}^{-1}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{jik})z_{ji}=(\\kappa_{jik}+\\lambda_{ij}^{-1})(\\kappa_{jik}+q^{-1}[\\lambda_{ij};0])\n\n(q^{-1}\\lambda_{ij}^{-1}-(q-q^{-1})\\kappa_{jik})z_{ik}=\\kappa_{jik}(\\lambda_{jk}^{-1}\\kappa_{jik}+[\\lambda_{ik};1])","source_id":"arXiv:1404.0305","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"f26113fa9cd7e436344e01e1908caf4a306eace0e09daf7371dceaad97320fe2","kind":"equation","label":"Equation 9","ref_key":"eq:kappa9","name":"","order":23,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.0305","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"6a006355f905f12b959f2888d2476ccc19dcd28369b459ced08a0fad4ae59ab4","line":611,"origin":"latex_env:equation","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:12:13+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":1137,"math_hints":169}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1404.0305","title":"Irreducible completely pointed modules of quantum groups of type $A$","abstract":"We give a classification of all irreducible completely pointed $U_q(\\mathfrak{sl}_{n+1})$ modules over a characteristic zero field in which $q$ is not a root of unity. This generalizes the classification result of Benkart, Britten and Lemire in the non quantum case. We also show that any infinite-dimensional irreducible completely pointed $U_q(\\mathfrak{sl}_{n+1})$ can be obtained from some irreducible completely pointed module over the quantized Weyl algebra $A_{n+1}^q$.","authors":["V. Futorny","J. Hartwig","E. Wilson"],"year":"2014","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.0305","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{},"macros_override":[]},"deps":[],"dependents":[]}